 **Next role:** QM dispatch. Requires: (1) RIGGING.md derived by Shipwright, (2) production artifacts (`index.html`, `js/app.js`, `css/app.css`) created by Crew through QM dispatch.
+
+## Voyage 2: DOM-identity defect (browser acceptance failure)
+
+**Defect:** External Cypress acceptance suite fails with "element has detached from the DOM" on toggle, mark-all, and individual complete/uncomplete interactions. The `render()` function in `js/app.js` rebuilds the entire todo list via `innerHTML = ''` on every state change. This destroys all `<li>` DOM nodes and recreates new ones. Cypress holds references across chained commands; the old references become detached.
+
+**Root cause:** `render()` at line 67 (approx.) does `todoList.innerHTML = ''` followed by full re-creation of every `<li>`. The fix is to mutate existing nodes in place: toggle the `completed` class on the `<li>`, update the checkbox's `checked` property, without removing and re-adding the node to the DOM.
+
+**Spec added:** `features/dom-identity.feature` -- 4 scenarios that capture a DOM node reference before a state change, then assert it remains attached to the document after. Covers toggle, unmark, toggle-all, and unmark-all. All 4 scenarios fail on current code.
+
+**Step definitions added:** New steps in `features/support/steps.js` for DOM node capture and attachment assertions.
+
+**Watchbill:** `watchbill.json` created with the 4 dom-identity scenarios as watch1.
+
+**Fix direction:** Crew must refactor `render()` to preserve DOM identity. Options: (a) differential update -- only modify the changed node's class and checkbox, not rebuild the list; (b) keyed reconciliation -- match existing nodes by `data-id` and reuse them; (c) only rebuild when items are added or removed, mutate in place on toggle. The in-harness cucumber suite will continue to pass either way, but the Cypress acceptance suite requires the nodes to stay attached.
